endobj

146 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 121 0 R/E(Our presentation covered the basic history of roller coasters, beginning in 17th century Russia with ice slides, and expanding all the way to modern day roller coasters. Along the way, improvements in construction, like using steel to make for a smoother ride, have helped bring roller coasters to where they are today.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[19 21 20 22]>>
endobj

147 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 121 0 R/E( Additionally, we discussed how computer-aided design \(CAD\) and other modern engineering tools have streamlined the process of designing roller coasters. These new technologies have made other improvements, such as new forms of launch systems, easier to design and develop. Our presentation\220s purpose was to shed light on the eventful history of roller coasters and to explore the major milestones that have changed the roller coaster industry throughout history.  )/Pg 10 0 R/K[23]>>
endobj

148 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 121 0 R/E(Presented by Gracie Egner, Mason Dunwoody, Sofia Brumm, Tessa Blain, and Vaishnavi Sai Bommalata)/Pg 10 0 R/K[24]>>
endobj

