endobj

479 0 obj
<</Title(Architecture is well known for making beautifully meticulous models of their buildings and the space around them. Often with makeshift material \(in the cases of architecture students\) like cardboard, paper, Styrofoam, and much more. On the THRILL theming team, we heavily take inspiration from this, by looking at the architectural models people have made, we can figure out what materials to use for the landscape and environment around the coaster. We have been making models of trees with clay, and we just began to make leaves with Styrofoam. Models make the product \(i.e. the building, in this case: the coaster\) seem cohesive with the environment and offers context and atmosphere. We are doing this in THRILL with making our environment inspired by a local urban legend, the Pope Lick. We are making the environment normal at first, but progressively more unsettling and immersive in the story, starting with the gas station. It may seem normal at first, but soon riders will see missing posters and feel the environment change to be eerie. Like in architecture, we are taking heavy inspiration from the site of Pope Lick itself, the gas station, the creek, the bridge. We are learning from the architecture around Louisville and hope to make a theme around the coaster that does the site and story justice.)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 450 0 R/Next 480 0 R>>
endobj

480 0 obj
