endobj

482 0 obj
<</Title(In 1983, Speigel founded the consulting firm ITPS. Over his career, Speigel has worked on more than 500 projects in over 55 countries and has contributed to the development and success of numerous attractions, including Kings Island and Kings Dominion. He has also served as chairman of the International Association of Amusement Parks and Attractions \(IAAPA\), one of the leading organizations in the global attractions industry. In recognition of his contributions, Dennis was inducted into the IAAPA Hall of Fame in 2022.)/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 415 0 R/Prev 452 0 R/Next 505 0 R>>
endobj

483 0 obj
<</Title(We are incredibly grateful to Dennis Speigel for taking the time to speak with THRILL and share his knowledge with our members. His experiences offered us insight into how everything within a theme park, from the hospitality to the rides themselves, is intertwined and work together to create the experience that guests have when they visit a park. From all the members at THRILL, we want to thank Dennis Speigel for being part of our journey as a student organization and for showing our members a real industry leader who is continuing to shape the entertainment industry today!)/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 415 0 R/Prev 505 0 R/Next 453 0 R>>
endobj

484 0 obj
<</Title(My name is AJ Wyckoff, and I am vice president of THRILL. My love for the industry dates back to 2018 when I went to Kings Island with my family and they took me on Mystic Timbers. The rest is history. I spent the rest of that summer I spent researching and looking up as many theme parks as I could, and I could not get enough of them. 3 years later, I got to go to Cedar Point with my family and from that day on I knew the combination of my love for math and roller coasters destined me to pursue mechanical engineering, which led me to the University of Louisville. I met Preston at Leadership Advantage, a pre-semester summer camp for incoming Speed School freshman, and he introduced this idea that would eventually become THRILL.)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 455 0 R/Next 485 0 R>>
endobj

485 0 obj
<</Title(The best thing about THRILL is that it is such a young and new RSO which means the precedent hasn't been set. All officers and members of THRILL can be as ambitious as we please because we are paving our own tracks for this club, and the sky's the limit. My plans and goals for THRILL are to expand past just the engineering aspect of THRILL. I feel as of now that most of our members are engineers, which is fantastic, but there's so much more to the industry. There's marketing, sales, and management, which I believe there are students on campus who would benefit and love to be a part of those aspects of the industry.)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 455 0 R/Prev 484 0 R>>
endobj

486 0 obj
<</Title(International Association of Amusement Parks and Attractions \(IAAPA\) Conference- November 16-19.)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 418 0 R/Prev 456 0 R/Next 506 0 R>>
endobj

487 0 obj
<</Title(Additionally, THRILL hosted its CoasterVille event in the new Engineering Student Success and Research Building \(ESSRB\). With over 100 UofL students attending this event, THRILL was able to educate the student body on how roller coasters work, the progress that has been made throughout history, and much more!)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 418 0 R/Prev 507 0 R/Next 457 0 R>>
endobj

