500 0 obj
<</Title(When Walt Disney was laying the foundation for Disneyland in the 50s, critics thought he was crazy thinking that his cartoon theme park would get anywhere. Now, the Disney theme parks are the most successful in the industry, fulfilling Disney's vision of becoming the blueprint for amusement parks in the future. Still, a lot goes into making sure "The Happiest Place on Earth" is running smoothly. Workers of all kinds of backgrounds are needed, like: cast members to interact with the guests, imagineers to make sure everything is safe, ride operators, food and merchandising staff, and so much more. Additionally, population control is a huge part of the success at the Disney Parks. Rides or experiences that have the capacity for lots of riders, along with a long wait for these rides are used strategically to help maintain population control in Disney. Experiences like the Monsters Inc. Laugh Floor has the capacity for lots of guests, making walkways near this attraction easier to navigate. Lastly, you need fun attractions to keep the guests coming back. Rise of the Resistance, for example, is a fan favorite, and also happens to have the most concrete poured for a Disney ride, AND is a trackless thrill ride, giving riders a smoother experience.)/Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/Parent 473 0 R>>
endobj

501 0 obj
<</Title(During CoasterVille, I hosted a booth about seasonal theme park haunt events such as Universal Studios\220 Halloween Horror Nights, Six Flags\220 Fright Fest, and Hersheypark\220s Dark Nights. These events take place starting in late August or mid-September and run until early November. At the center of these events are several different haunted houses and scare zones, each with their own theming. Theming is often based on pop culture horror icons, common fears and phobias, or folklore monsters.)/Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Parent 477 0 R/Next 510 0 R>>
endobj

502 0 obj
<</Title(October 2026)/Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Parent 477 0 R/Prev 511 0 R>>
endobj

503 0 obj
<</Title(THEMED RIDES INDUSTRY LEADERS OF LOUISVILLE)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 478 0 R/Next 504 0 R>>
endobj

504 0 obj
<</Title(Roller Coaster Trains)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 478 0 R/Prev 503 0 R/First 512 0 R/Last 513 0 R/Count -2>>
endobj

505 0 obj
<</Title(During his visit, THRILL members had the opportunity to hear about Speigel\220s extensive industry experience and learn more about how to have a career in the theme park industry. He advised that the best place to get started is simply wherever you can. He noted that something as small as taking tickets, like he did, could be the start to a successful career in this industry.)/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 415 0 R/Prev 482 0 R/Next 483 0 R>>
endobj

506 0 obj
<</Title(As the month of October ends, THRILL recaps a wonderful third month of the fall semester.)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 418 0 R/Prev 486 0 R/Next 507 0 R>>
endobj

507 0 obj
<</Title(This month, THRILL hosted guest speaker Dennis Speigel. From Speigel, members of THRILL received information on the details of the roller coaster and theme park industry, along with his own experiences across his extensive career.)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 418 0 R/Prev 506 0 R/Next 487 0 R>>
endobj

