510 0 obj
<</Title(One of my favorite topics that I got to share with CoasterVille attendees was the art of scare acting and the considerations that designers and engineers take to keep them safe. Anyone can audition to be a scare actor, and since actors are primarily cast based on height, body type, and experience, the audition process is very simple. I asked three volunteers from each group to tell me their name, age, and height, spin slowly to give a full view of their body type, and then state their favorite scary movie. That is a very common audition structure, even for massively popular events.)/Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Parent 477 0 R/Prev 501 0 R/Next 511 0 R>>
endobj

511 0 obj
<</Title(Several precautions are taken in the process of constructing haunted houses in order to keep these actors from getting hit by guests who can\220t control their fear reaction well. Actors will often perform scares from behind walls or screens, on top of stages, or within fenced off areas. Actors are also usually taught to perform their jump scare very quickly and remove themself as soon as they\220re finished. This can keep them from being the victim of a physically violent guest. These safeguards are not always foolproof though, especially for a roaming actor in a scare zone. More effective solutions for actor safety are still developing within the industry.)/Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Parent 477 0 R/Prev 510 0 R/Next 502 0 R>>
endobj

512 0 obj
<</Title(At CoasterVille, I gave a presentation on coaster trains. It covered the different types of trains, the restraints that keep riders in their seats, and the safety mechanisms working behind the scenes. Those include ratchet and hydraulic locks, anti-rollback dogs on the lift hill, and sensors that confirm every restraint is locked before a train can leave the station. It was a lot of fun showing people just how many layers of protection go into a roller coaster, especially with all of the recent horrific events in the news.)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 504 0 R/Next 513 0 R>>
endobj

513 0 obj
<</Title(That mattered to me because incidents at theme parks are actually really rare, and I wanted people to leave understanding that. When you see how many backups exist for the backups, it\220s a lot easier to feel safe on a ride. This topic was extremely important to me because I love roller coasters so much. These machines are built for riders\220 enjoyment, and I hate the idea that anyone would feel unsafe on them.)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 504 0 R/Prev 512 0 R>>
endobj

